20:34.280 --> 20:34.720
Corollary.

20:34.860 --> 20:36.500
For a cyclic group of order N,

20:36.640 --> 20:38.260
we have A-I equal to A-J,

20:38.800 --> 20:41.740
if and only if I is equal to J plus N-K.

20:42.520 --> 20:44.240
So, that's basically how it goes, right?

20:45.300 --> 20:45.740
Corollary.

20:45.860 --> 20:47.440
If G is a group,

20:48.300 --> 20:49.360
and A is an element of G,

20:49.460 --> 20:51.680
then the order of A is actually the order

20:51.680 --> 20:53.400
of the subgroup generated by A.

20:53.880 --> 20:54.820
That's very important,

20:54.920 --> 20:56.220
that connects the order of the element

20:56.220 --> 20:58.180
to the order of the group generated by that element.

20:58.800 --> 21:00.620
We use that all the time.

21:01.800 --> 21:02.200
Corollary.

21:02.460 --> 21:03.320
If G is a group,

21:03.840 --> 21:05.180
and A is an element of G,

21:05.620 --> 21:06.860
with the order of A being N,

21:07.600 --> 21:08.080
well then,

21:08.180 --> 21:09.980
if A to the power of K is equal to E,

21:10.380 --> 21:13.220
it must be that N divides K.

21:13.780 --> 21:14.960
K has to be a multiple

21:14.960 --> 21:17.620
of the order of A,

21:17.800 --> 21:19.640
if A to the power of K is equal to E.

21:19.980 --> 21:20.120
Alright?

21:21.120 --> 21:21.520
Now,

21:22.620 --> 21:24.000
