21:24.300 --> 21:25.240
It's the corollary, right?

21:25.240 --> 21:26.620
A is in G,

21:26.820 --> 21:27.740
the order of A is N,

21:28.520 --> 21:30.620
and A to the K is equal to E,

21:30.740 --> 21:32.340
and then A to the K is equal to A to the zero,

21:33.420 --> 21:33.760
right?

21:34.260 --> 21:34.860
But then,

21:34.960 --> 21:36.720
N must divide K minus zero,

21:37.520 --> 21:38.500
hence N divides K.

21:39.040 --> 21:39.280
Yay.

21:39.760 --> 21:40.700
Alright, that wasn't bad.

21:41.660 --> 21:41.940
Theorem.

21:43.680 --> 21:44.040
Theorem.

21:45.500 --> 21:46.480
If G is a group,

21:46.700 --> 21:47.820
and A is an element of G,

21:48.420 --> 21:49.560
and the order of A is N,

21:50.280 --> 21:51.540
