21:51.540 --> 21:55.840
then the subgroup generated by A to the power of K

21:55.840 --> 21:58.980
is equal to the subgroup generated by A

21:58.980 --> 22:01.020
to the greatest common divisor of N and K.

22:02.040 --> 22:02.360
Alright?

22:02.720 --> 22:03.080
So,

22:04.120 --> 22:04.560
you know,

22:04.740 --> 22:06.240
obvious corollary here,

22:06.420 --> 22:09.800
if K and N are relatively prime,

22:10.360 --> 22:12.560
then A to the K is equal to A to the one.

22:13.220 --> 22:13.900
In other words,

22:13.980 --> 22:15.080
you get another generator, right?

22:15.160 --> 22:16.400
But this is more general than that.

22:16.400 --> 22:19.060
More than that,

22:19.300 --> 22:20.060
A to the power of K,

22:20.600 --> 22:22.360
the order of that element is N

22:22.360 --> 22:25.480
divided by the greatest common divisor of N and K.

22:29.080 --> 22:31.200
